  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — that A has a greater probability (67%) of yielding 0 Euros (unfavorable outcome) than B (66%) — implies that A is more right-skewed according to the stated definition. Therefore, the reason would prefer A. However, the individual chose B, not A. The individual’s justification is based entirely on the 1% higher probability of winning in B and the small difference in payoff, not on any consideration of skewness or distributional asymmetry. There is no mention of the 0 Euro outcomes or their probabilities in the justification. Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation process. The individual did not consider the skewness of the lotteries as defined in the reason. The final choice is based on a different criterion — a marginal increase in winning probability — not on skewness. Thus, the decision reason was not applied.",
