  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (skewness) is not considered by the individual. The individual focuses only on the absolute prize difference and the probability of winning, not on the distribution of outcomes or the proportion of probability assigned to unfavorable outcomes. Specifically, Lottery A has 80% chance of 0 Euros (higher than B's 75%), meaning it is more right-skewed. The decision reason would thus prefer A, but the individual chooses B based on a 5% higher probability of winning. This is inconsistent with the skewness-based reason. The individual’s justification does not reference skewness or the structure of the probability distribution. Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The individual’s reasoning is based on probability of winning, not on skewness. Hence, the decision reason was not applied.",
